{{DISPLAYTITLE:<span style="color: #ffa31a;">Barbarian Hut</span>}}
{{Protection}}{{MagicWords}}

{{Card Infobox|Cost=6|Rarity=Rare|Type=Building|Arena=Jungle Arena|ReleaseDate=4 January 2016}}
{{Quote|Building that periodically spawns Barbarians to fight the enemy. Time to make the Barbarians!}}

The Barbarian Hut is a {{Rarity|Rare}} [[Cards|card]] that is unlocked from the [[Arenas|Jungle Arena (Arena 9)]]. It spawns a [[:Category:Building Cards|building]] with high hitpoints. Every 15 seconds, the Barbarian Hut will passively summon a group of three [[Barbarians]], with a 0.5 seconds delay from each other. When defeated, it will also spawn a Barbarian. It appears as a wooden hut with a team-colored roof and a sword hoisted above the entrance, along with a keg of [[Elixir]] for decoration beside it. A Barbarian Hut card costs 6 Elixir to deploy.

==Modifiers==
===[[File:Barbarian Hut Common Modifier.png|45x45px]] Common: Best of Both Barbs===
{{Quote|+100% spawn rate}}
Barbarians spawn twice as frequently.

===[[File:Barbarian Hut Rare Modifier.png|45x45px]] Rare: Extra Elitists===
{{Quote|Spawns Elite Barbarians}}
Each spawn cycle sends out 2 [[Elite Barbarians]] instead of regular Barbarians.

===[[File:Barbarian Hut Epic Modifier.png|45x45px]] Epic: Well, ****!===
{{Quote|Mini Mega Knight Hut}}
Each spawn cycle sends out 1 small [[Mega Knight]] instead of regular Barbarians.

==Strategy==
{{Battle Deck with Card|:Category:Battle Decks using the Barbarian Hut Card}}
*The continual spawning of the Barbarians from the Barbarian Hut in affiliation with [[Tombstone]]s and [[Goblin Hut]]s can destroy an opposing [[:Category:Tower Troop Cards|Crown Tower]] if they are overlooked by the opponent. Placing down many huts like this is known as the Spawner strategy and can overwhelm opponents at all levels though some opponents can defend this strategy easily sometimes using [[Poison]] or [[Fireball]].
*The Barbarian Hut can be used defensively and deployed in front of the player's Crown Tower in order to protect it, do be careful, Your opponent may use [[:Category:Spell Cards|spells]] for some value on the Crown Towers.
*The player should be careful when using the Barbarian Hut as it may render them defenseless against an opponent's attack due to its high [[Elixir]] cost, so have some cheap [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] just in case.
*The Barbarian Hut can spawn up to 8 Barbarians (value of 8 Elixir), creating a maximum profit of 2 Elixir.
**Due to the high cost of placing a Barbarian Hut down and the total time it takes for the hut to create its maximum profit of Elixir, it is highly advised to protect the Barbarian Hut so that potential and Elixir profit is maximized.
**With its difficulty to maximize efficiency, an opposing player can easily throw a high damage spell card to greatly reduce the efficiency and the amount of spawned Barbarians. A [[Rocket]] will completely destroy the Barbarian Hut, but will be unable to prevent the first wave and its death spawn.
*Barbarians cannot target flying troops, so the Barbarian Hut can be destroyed by [[Minions]], [[Bats]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[Skeleton Dragons]], [[Mega Minion]], [[Electro Dragon]], or the [[Flying Machine]] unhindered if placed incorrectly outside a Crown Tower's range.
*The [[Bowler]] is a great counter to the Barbarian Hut, due to his damage and him knocking back each wave of Barbarians and stopping while doing so, allowing him to move more slowly and stay on the map longer and defend more troops.
*Even though it spawns Barbarians very slowly, do not underestimate it; it can deal heavy damage to or even destroy a Crown Tower.
*Since the [[:Category:Building Cards|building]] spawns Barbarians in groups of 3, it is very easy for splash damage troops or buildings to wipe them out one after one. When using the Barbarian Hut, try to take out area damage cards as quickly as possible. Alternatively, use fast troops with high health (e.g., [[Dark Prince]], [[Prince]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Boss Bandit]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Lumberjack]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A]], or [[Hog Rider]]) to briefly soak up some damage.
*A Barbarian Hut can stop a lone [[Mega Knight]] for a +1 Elixir trade. The 1 Barbarian which spawn upon the building's destruction will survive but will not be very useful.
*In rare situations, a [[Balloon]] can snipe a Barbarian Hut placed in the center of the opponent's side. It will easily destroy the Barbarian Hut for a +1 Elixir trade, without it being distracted by the spawned Barbarians or vice versa. However, this should only be done if the player lacks better counters.
*The [[Miner]] can be a slightly effective counter to this card, as he gives an almost 3 Elixir trade advantage. However, the Miner will not completely destroy it, and it will be able to spawn 2 waves of Barbarians before it runs out of health. Due to this, it might just be a good idea to not play a Miner, as the Barbarian Hut will be able to still summon 6 Barbarians for a 4 Elixir trade disadvantage, and they will be grouped up, making them a more effective potential counterpush.
**The [[Goblin Barrel]] is ineffective against the Barbarian Hut as it may not do much damage, especially if a wave of Barbarians come out just in time.
*The Barbarian Hut is affected by [[Rage]], technically allowing it to produce extra waves. However, its lifetime decays more quickly under a Rage spell's effect, and as a result, no extra wave will be produced with the help of Rage. However, it will result in the last wave spawning 3 Barbarians instead of 1. This is a 2 Elixir investment for an equivalent return value of 2 Elixir, and thus it can be worth using if the player wants to make use of the last wave of Barbarians in defense.
*In the [[Global Spell|Rage Challenge]], all buildings' (including the Barbarian Hut's) lifetimes are unaffected, but in Barbarian Hut's case, the Troop producing speed is, allowing it to produce up to 3 waves of Barbarians instead of the usual 2.33 in the challenge.

