==Trivia==
*The word "''Barbarian''" comes from the Greek "''βάρβαρος''" (''bárbaros''), meaning foreign. Dating back to the ancient Greek times, the Greeks referred to non-Greek people as barbarians because the language they spoke sounded to Greeks like gibberish represented by the sounds “bar…bar…;”.
**The Barbarian Hut is 1 of 6 [[cards]] associated with [[Barbarians]], with the others being [[Elite Barbarians]], [[Barbarian Launcher]], [[Battle Ram]], [[Barbarian Barrel]], and of course, Barbarians.
*The Barbarian Hut closely resembles the Level 1 Barracks from Clash of Clans, only that it now has a blue roof; however, from the enemy's point of view, it is red. The Barbarian Hut also has a small hole in the roof that the Barracks does not have, a keg of [[Elixir]], and is more reinforced. Level 1 Barracks also only allow the training of Barbarians.
*The Barbarian Hut, along with [[Elixir Collector]] and [[X-Bow]], are the most expensive [[:Category:Building Cards|buildings]], costing 6 Elixir.
*Among all buildings that can spawn troops, the Barbarian Hut has the lowest spawn speed of all buildings, with an spawn speed of 13.5 seconds.
*In the Norwegian, Finnish, and Vietnamese language settings of the game, the Barbarian Hut's name translates to "Barbarian Cabin", "Barbarian Lodge", and "Barbarian Tent" respectively.
*The Barbarian Hut is one of the first building cards to be featured in a [[Training Camp|Trainer]]'s [[Battle Decks|deck]], alongside the [[Cannon]], [[Goblin Hut]], [[Tombstone]], [[Bomb Tower]], and [[Inferno Tower]].
*Though not the first cards to receive balance changes, the Barbarian Hut is one of the first {{Rarity|Rare}} cards to ever receive balance changes since the [[Version History#February 2016 Update (2/2/2016)|February 2016 Update]], the others are the [[Wizard]], Bomb Tower, Inferno Tower, and Elixir Collector.
*The Barbarian Hut is 1 of 23 cards that has had its Elixir cost changed, the others being [[Bomber]], [[Fire Spirit]], [[Royal Recruits]], Cannon, [[Mortar]], [[Musketeer]], [[Three Musketeers]], [[Heal]], Goblin Hut, Bomb Tower, [[Furnace]], Elixir Collector, [[Skeleton Army]], [[P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Electro Giant]], [[Bowler]], [[Goblin Barrel]], [[Barbarian Barrel]], [[Rage]], [[Fisherman]], and the [[Monk]].
*The Barbarian Hut is unavailable in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special gamemodes]]. More specifically:
**It is 1 of 20 cards that is unavailable in [[Mirror]] mode, the others being [[Minions]], Cannon, Mortar, [[Tesla]], Goblin Hut, Tombstone, Bomb Tower, Inferno Tower, Furnace, Elixir Collector, [[Freeze]], [[Clone]], X-Bow, [[Golden Knight]], [[Skeleton King]], [[Archer Queen]], [[Mighty Miner]], [[Little Prince]], and the Monk.
**It is unavailable in [[Global Spell|The Floor is Healing]] sub-[[:Category:Modes|mode]] of the Global Spell game mode, much like other building cards, as well as the [[Cannon Cart]].
*Before the Barbarian Hut's card release, the Barbarian Hut's cost was increased to 7 Elixir (from 6 Elixir), its hitpoints were increased by 42%, its spawn time interval was increased to 14 seconds (from 11.85 seconds), the Barbarians' hitpoints were increased by 24%, and their damage was decreased by 12%.

